+++ b/INTEGRATION_NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,197 @@
+# vLLM × DFlash × DDTree — Integration Notes
+
+> Phase 2 design document. Tracks the design decisions before code changes.
+> Base: vLLM PR #41703 (`refs/pull/41703/head`, Gemma-4 dflash temporary build).
+> Target model: `google/gemma-4-E2B-it`.
+
+## Decisions (locked)
+
+| # | Decision |
+|---|---|
+| Integration depth | **Option C — staged**. New `DDTreeProposer(DFlashProposer)` subclass + new config flag `ddtree_enabled` (default `False`). When off, the new class is not instantiated at all → token-bit-exact with current dflash. |
+| Target attention backend | `--attention-backend triton_attn`, with `speculative-config.attention_backend = "flash_attn"` (per dflash README for Gemma-4 PR). |
+| Source layout | Local branch in this `vllm` clone (`feature/ddtree`). Push to `github.com/kimwin2/<repo>`. Upstream vLLM not touched. |
+| Packaging | Port the three needed ddtree primitives into vLLM as `vllm/v1/spec_decode/ddtree_utils.py` (attribution preserved, MIT). ddtree repo itself is not added as a runtime dependency. |
+| Baseline | `google/gemma-4-E2B-it` target + dflash draft (whichever HF id is paired in the dflash recipe). |
+
+## What DDTree changes
+
+DDTree replaces dflash's flat N-token draft with a **diffusion draft tree**:
+
+1. Run the dflash draft model once over `block_size` positions (same as today).
+2. Take the per-position logits from the draft model.
+3. Heap-expand a top-k tree of `tree_budget` nodes (`build_ddtree_tree`).
+4. Verify the whole tree in **one target forward** using a 2D visibility mask.
+5. Follow the verified posterior along the tree to find the longest accepted chain (`follow_verified_tree`).
+
+In a vLLM-shaped pipeline this maps onto:
+
+| Stage | vLLM today | With DDTree |
+|---|---|---|
+| Draft model forward | `DFlashProposer.propose → model(...)` | Unchanged |
+| Draft selection per spec position | `_greedy_sample` (argmax) | Heap-expand tree from per-position logits |
+| Target verify | Linear: target sees `1+N` packed queries per request, non-causal | Tree: target sees `1+tree_budget` queries per request with a 2D visibility mask |
+| Accept | Linear cumprod compare on draft vs sampled | Walk tree on sampled posterior |
+
+## Staging plan
+
+### Step C0 — Scaffolding (zero behavior change when off)
+
+Files added:
+
+- `vllm/v1/spec_decode/ddtree_utils.py` — ported, dependency-free primitives:
+  - `build_ddtree_tree(draft_logits, budget) -> (node_token_ids, node_depths, parents, child_maps, visibility, build_subtimes)`
+  - `compile_ddtree_tree(...)` (kept for completeness; not used in C1)
+  - `follow_verified_tree(child_maps, posterior) -> (accepted_indices, next_token)` (used in C2)
+- `vllm/v1/spec_decode/ddtree_proposer.py` — `DDTreeProposer(DFlashProposer)`:
+  - Adds `ddtree_budget`, `ddtree_enabled`, logging on construction
+  - C0: `propose()` delegates to `super().propose()` (no diff)
+
+Files edited:
+
+- `vllm/config/speculative.py` — add two fields and a helper:
+  - `ddtree_enabled: bool = False`
+  - `ddtree_budget: int | None = None` (defaults to `num_speculative_tokens` when on)
+  - `def use_ddtree(self) -> bool` → `self.use_dflash() and self.ddtree_enabled`
+- `vllm/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py` — at the `use_dflash()` branch, instantiate
+  `DDTreeProposer` instead of `DFlashProposer` when `use_ddtree()` is true. All
+  `isinstance(self.drafter, DFlashProposer)` checks throughout the file continue to
+  succeed via subclass.
+
+Off-path guarantee: `ddtree_enabled` defaults to `False`. With no
+`"ddtree_enabled": true` in `--speculative-config`, the new class is never
+imported or instantiated, the new config helper short-circuits, and the
+runtime path is structurally identical to upstream PR #41703.
+
+### Step C1 — Draft-side tree, linear verify
+
+`DDTreeProposer.propose()` overrides the base by:
+
+1. Calling the standard base flow (`set_inputs_first_pass`,
+   `build_per_group_and_layer_attn_metadata`, model forward) — unchanged.
+2. At the point where the base does `_greedy_sample`, compute the **full
+   logits** at the `B × N` spec positions via `self.model.compute_logits`.
+3. For each request, reshape its `N × V` logits into `[N, V]`, then call
+   `build_ddtree_tree(logits, budget=ddtree_budget)`.
+4. Return the linear top-1 path of the tree as the `[B, N]` int tensor. The
+   top-1 path of the tree is identical to per-position argmax, so the
+   **token result is bit-identical to dflash-only**. This makes C1 a
+   regression test: the tree code path runs end-to-end without changing
+   serving output. Tree statistics (`size`, `max depth`) are emitted via
+   `logger.debug` per request.
+
+C1 deliverables: the tree build path is exercised under load. Acceptance
+length and tokens-per-second should match dflash-only baselines within
+measurement noise.
+
+### Step C2 — Tree verify (future, stubbed)
+
+Three coupled changes required:
+
+1. **Query expansion**: in `set_inputs_first_pass`, expand per-request query
+   from `1 + num_speculative_tokens` to `1 + tree_budget`. Reuse the
+   existing `copy_and_expand_dflash_inputs_kernel` pattern but write
+   tree-shaped node ids (root + flattened tree) and tree depth positions.
+2. **2D visibility mask on the target verify pass**: the visibility matrix
+   from `build_ddtree_tree` (`tree_budget+1` square) must flow into the
+   target attention metadata for the **target** forward (not the draft).
+   This needs the attention backend to support a custom 2D mask per
+   request. Spec'd backends:
+   - `flash_attn` with `mask_mod`/`block_mask` (FlexAttention path) — verify
+     availability on PR #41703.
+   - Fallback: `triton_attn` with a custom mask buffer (extra kernel work).
+3. **Tree follow accept**: replace the cumprod-style acceptance in the
+   rejection sampler with `follow_verified_tree` on the sampled posterior,
+   then map the accepted indices back into the KV cache compaction. The
+   current `compact_dynamic_cache` from ddtree is unusable as-is (it
+   targets HF `DynamicCache`), but the equivalent paged-block compaction
+   already exists in the dflash drafter and can be parameterized by the
+   accepted index tensor instead of a contiguous prefix length.
+
+C2 is gated behind the same `ddtree_enabled` flag and falls back to C1
+behavior (linear verify) if the chosen attention backend does not
+advertise custom-mask support — emitting a warning, not a hard failure.
+
+## Config surface (added to `SpeculativeConfig`)
+
+```jsonc
+{
+  "method": "dflash",
+  "model": "z-lab/gemma-4-E2B-it-DFlash",   // example, paired model
+  "num_speculative_tokens": 15,
+  "attention_backend": "flash_attn",
+  "ddtree_enabled": true,                    // default false
+  "ddtree_budget": 24                        // default = num_speculative_tokens
+}
+```
+
+When `ddtree_enabled` is omitted/false: zero behavior change.
+
+## Files touched
+
+| Path | Action | One-line summary |
+|---|---|---|
+| `vllm/v1/spec_decode/ddtree_utils.py` | add | Port of `build_ddtree_tree` / `compile_ddtree_tree` / `follow_verified_tree` (MIT, attributed). |
+| `vllm/v1/spec_decode/ddtree_proposer.py` | add | `DDTreeProposer(DFlashProposer)`, C0 scaffold + C1 tree-build hook. |
+| `vllm/config/speculative.py` | edit | `ddtree_enabled`, `ddtree_budget`, `use_ddtree()`. |
+| `vllm/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py` | edit | Instantiate `DDTreeProposer` when `use_ddtree()`. |
+| `INTEGRATION_NOTES.md` | add | This file. |
+
+## Dependencies and build
+
+No new third-party packages. ddtree's MIT primitives are vendored inside
+vLLM with attribution at the top of `ddtree_utils.py`. The standalone
+ddtree repo cloned next to this one is reference-only and not on
+`PYTHONPATH`.
+
+Build/install procedure is **unchanged** vs. PR #41703. Standard:
+
+```bash
+VLLM_USE_PRECOMPILED=1 uv pip install -e . --torch-backend=auto
+```
+
+## Server commands
+
+### DFlash-only (regression baseline; ddtree off)
+
+```bash
+vllm serve google/gemma-4-E2B-it \
+  --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 \
+  --speculative-config '{"method": "dflash", "model": "<paired-dflash-draft>", "num_speculative_tokens": 15, "attention_backend": "flash_attn"}' \
+  --attention-backend triton_attn \
+  --max-num-batched-tokens 32768 \
+  --trust-remote-code
+```
+
+### DFlash + DDTree (new path)
+
+```bash
+vllm serve google/gemma-4-E2B-it \
+  --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 \
+  --speculative-config '{"method": "dflash", "model": "<paired-dflash-draft>", "num_speculative_tokens": 15, "attention_backend": "flash_attn", "ddtree_enabled": true, "ddtree_budget": 24}' \
+  --attention-backend triton_attn \
+  --max-num-batched-tokens 32768 \
+  --trust-remote-code
+```
+
+C1 result expectation: identical tokens to the baseline (tree code runs but
+returns top-1 path). C2 result expectation (future): same tokens or higher
+acceptance length depending on whether the tree improved the accept rate.
+
+## Known limits / future work
+
+- C2 verify-side path is **stubbed**, not implemented. The flag flips on the
+  tree-build but does not yet plumb the 2D mask into the target attention
+  metadata. Wiring needs to be paired with concrete backend capability
+  checks (flash_attn block mask path on Gemma-4 PR).
+- Batch > 1 with per-request 2D masks: ddtree's reference code is strictly
+  batch=1. The per-request tree shape (budget) is fixed, so a constant
+  `(1+budget, 1+budget)` mask block per request is straightforward, but
+  needs benchmarking against linear dflash on the realistic Gemma-4-E2B
+  serving batch size.
+- KV cache compaction for the tree-rejected branches in vLLM's paged-block
+  layout reuses the existing dflash slot mapping rather than ddtree's
+  `compact_dynamic_cache` (HF DynamicCache-specific).
+- Tree statistics logging is per-request `logger.debug`; promote to a Prom
+  metric (`ddtree_tree_size`, `ddtree_max_depth`, `ddtree_accept_len`) once
+  C2 lands.
